{
  "diagnosis": "The FIFO violates the valid_matches_occupancy property in two ways. First, when a simultaneous push/pop occurs with count=1, the combinational m_valid (computed from current count=1) is 1, but the count register updates to 1 (unchanged), so the post-edge occupancy is 1; however, if the pre-edge count were 0 and a simultaneous push/pop is attempted, m_valid=0 prevents pop, so this is not the issue. The real bug is the count update for the 2'b11 case: it incorrectly increments count (count <= count + 1) instead of keeping it unchanged. This causes count to grow beyond actual occupancy when push and pop happen together, making m_valid assert high when the FIFO is actually empty. Second, s_ready uses m_valid in its expression, creating combinational feedback because m_valid depends on count, which is updated by push/pop that depend on s_ready. The fix is to correct the 2'b11 case to hold count steady and rewrite s_ready without referencing m_valid.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "file": "rtl/packet_queue.sv",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 16,
      "replacement": "    assign s_ready = !rst && (count < DEPTH || (count != 0 && m_ready));"
    },
    {
      "file": "rtl/packet_queue.sv",
      "start_line": 35,
      "end_line": 35,
      "replacement": "            2'b11: count <= count;"
    }
  ]
}
